<title>USA: Santa Fe Pacific expanding Nevada mine.</title>
<headline>Santa Fe Pacific expanding Nevada mine.</headline>
<dateline>ALBUQUERQUE, N.M. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santa Fe Pacific Gold Corp said on Wednesday that it has received government approval to expand its Lone Tree Mine in Nevada.</p>
<p>The new section to be mined is expected to produce 10,000 ounces of gold in the current fourth quarter ending December 31.</p>
<p>Including the new production, Lone Tree is expected to produce 185,000 to 195,000 ounces of gold at a cash cost of between $255 and $265 per ounce in 1996, the company said. The approval was granted by the federal Bureau of Land Management.</p>
</text>
